\label{L:balls}
Notation as above.
If $[0,1]\cap\mathbb{Q}\subseteq \bigcup_{j,k} I_{j}^k$, then $K$ is $S$-norm-Euclidean.

Consider the field $K=\mathbb{Q}(\sqrt{-67})$
and choose $\{2,3\}$.
We write down the intervals $I_j^k$ with $0\leq j\leq k\leq 4$ and $\gcd(j,k)=1$,
and check that these cover the unit interval.  Thus $K$ is $S$-norm-Euclidean.
Figure~\ref{fig2} gives the intervals $I_j^k$ and the corresponding covering of $\mathcal{F}$.
We have sorted the intervals to make it easier to ``see'' them in the covering.
































